<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa rand hits 4.50 vs dlr on fx easing nerves.</title>
<headline>S.Africa rand hits 4.50 vs dlr on fx easing nerves.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rand was bid at 4.5000 against the dollar on Monday, its weakest level since February 5, 1997.</p>
<p>Dealers said the unit came under pressure against a weak dollar, hit by demand for dollars out of London and nervousness ahead of the relaxation of exchange controls on individuals on July 1.  </p>
<p>At 1005 GMT the unit was bid at 4.5050/80 against the dollar from 4.4830/60 on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
